WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.550
Southwark, London, 1974.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:10.450
The Heygate estate is completed:
1,212 homes for about 3,000 people.

3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.070
By the late 1990s, a survey
found it structurally sound,

4
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.010
but in need of complete refurbishment.

5
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.950
Today it's gone.

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.230
A plan approved in 2013 included
3,000 new homes on the site.

7
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.570
Places like this can look run-down, yet
be too expensive for the people who grew

8
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.050
up there.

9
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.530
How can both be true?

10
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.330
In this mission, you'll explore
poor inner-city housing,

11
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.590
and what follows when
an estate is demolished.

12
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.590
Then you'll read a
chart of New York rents,

13
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.070
and work out who wins and who loses.

14
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:48.450
Your mission: explain how one area can
be both run-down and too expensive for

15
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:49.950
the people who grew up there.
